304 0 obj
<<
/Title (Ans-> Average, Gaussian, and Median filters all smooth images but work differently. The Average Filter replaces each pixel with the plain mean of its neighborhood, causing heavy blurring of edges. The Gaussian Filter uses a weighted average \(more weight to center pixels\), giving smoother results with better edge preservation. The Median Filter replaces each pixel with the median value of its neighborhood, making it ideal for removing salt-and-pepper noise without blurring edges much, unlike the other two.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 203 0 R
>>
